  "body": "We could possibly eliminate this and always wait for startedPromise. That would mean advanceQueue is always asynchronous.\n\nTwo questions:\n1. Would such a change be observable to current code? If so, how?\n2. Assuming that it is observable, what would be the perf hit in realistic situations?\n\nMy guess for 1 is that it would make the underlying sink's write() always called asynchronously (which fixes #135, for one).\n",
